course: dictionary
lesson: 8436
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, look at the words around it. «Her parents made sacrifices so she could go to college.» Here a sacrifice is something you give up that you value, because the sentence is about money and time given up for someone else.
explain: The same word can mean something different in a game. In chess, a sacrifice means giving up a piece on purpose to gain an advantage later. Ask yourself: what is this text about? The subject tells you which meaning to choose.
explain: Check your choice by putting it into the sentence. As a verb, sacrifice means to give up something valuable for a reason: «She sacrificed her free time to practise the violin.» If your meaning fits the sentence, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Sacrifice (noun) means giving up something you value for something more important or for someone else.
fact: Sacrifice (verb) means to give up something valuable for a reason.
fact: In chess, a sacrifice means giving up a piece on purpose to gain an advantage later.
fact: In old religions, a sacrifice meant killing an animal or offering something to a god.
fact: In baseball, a «sacrifice» play gets the batter out but moves a runner on.
exercise: «Her parents made sacrifices so she could go to college.» What does sacrifices mean here? | Lessons at school | Rules that stop you playing | *Things given up for someone else | Presents bought for a birthday
exercise: In chess, Sam gives up a rook on purpose to win later. What is this called? | Starting again | *A sacrifice | Cheating | Forgetting the rules
exercise: «She sacrificed her free time to practise the violin.» What does sacrificed mean? | Sold it for money | Lost it by accident | *Gave up something she valued for a reason | Found more of it
test: «The soldier made the ultimate sacrifice.» What does this mean? | *He died while serving his country | He gave his friend a special gift | He moved house to a new town | He won a medal for running
test: Which form shows that something happened in the past: sacrifice, sacrifices, sacrificed or sacrificing? | *sacrificed | sacrificing | sacrifices | sacrifice
exam: Mia gives up her Saturday to help her brother move house. What is this? | Cheating | A holiday | *A sacrifice | A competition
